net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: log the assigned random MAC address

The pending MediaTek patch passes a net_device pointer to %pM, printing
the first six bytes of the structure instead of the address. Report
dev_addr without changing address assignment or its fallback behavior.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -5369,7 +5369,7 @@
 		/* If the mac address is invalid, use random mac address */
 		eth_hw_addr_random(eth->netdev[i]);
 		dev_err(eth->dev, "generated random MAC address %pM\n",
-			eth->netdev[i]);
+			eth->netdev[i]->dev_addr);
 	}
 
 	return 0;
